      <div style="margin-top:28px">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px">Split PDF vs Organize Pages — which tool to use</h2>
        <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;line-height:1.75;margin:0">Use Split PDF when you want to divide one PDF into multiple separate files — for example, page 1 becomes file 1, pages 2–5 become file 2, and so on. Use Organize Pages when you want to stay within a single PDF but need to reorder, delete, or rotate pages within it. For the most control, organize the pages first, then split the result into the separate files you need.</p>
